.superpowers/
# writeJsonFileAtomic's temp siblings, `<path>.tmp-<pid>-<hrtime>`. A hard kill
# between the write and the rename orphans one, and for .mcp.json it holds
# resolved MCP server secrets -- nothing must ever commit that (ahood-cli#125).
# Every caller of that helper writes a *.json destination, so scoping the rule
# to .json keeps it from shadowing unrelated files someone happens to name
# `foo.tmp-1`; no leading slash, so it also covers .claude/skills.lock.json's.
*.json.tmp-*
